# Left-recursive grammar for left-associative addition.
#
# This is the natural way to express left-associativity: the recursive
# call sits on the left of the alternative. Standard PEG semantics
# reject this because a naive top-down parser enters an infinite
# descent at the same input position.
#
# Current behaviour in zpars:
#   - `zpars check`     flags Expr as left-recursive (validator diagnostic).
#   - `zpars vm`        blows the VM call stack.
#   - `zpars vm -p`     runs the Warth-style packrat VM, which handles it.
#                       Try: zpars vm -p examples/leftrec.peg "1+2+3"
#   - Matcher (no -p)   bails out at max_depth and returns no match.
Expr <- Expr "+" Num / Num
Num  <- [0-9]+
